[CHOSEN, not recovered] vkd3d-shader 2.1 patch for the native clients (LGPL-2.1+, as vkd3d).
Fix the constant comparison added by 0009: only declared components and their
active scalar width belong to the value. A scalar uint initializes four bytes,
not all four eight-byte union slots. Comparing the unused bytes prevented equal
array-index constants from merging, so identical bone-matrix loads stayed live
in separate registers and exhausted even vs_3_0's 32 temporaries.
Compare active representations, preserving signed zero and NaN payloads. This
changes neither shader source nor requested profile (kr4uzi/OpenBF2#36).

--- a/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
@@ -7048,7 +7048,16 @@
         {
             const struct hlsl_ir_constant *x = hlsl_ir_constant((struct hlsl_ir_node *)a), *y = hlsl_ir_constant((struct hlsl_ir_node *)b);
+            size_t component_size;
 
-            return !memcmp(&x->value, &y->value, sizeof(x->value));
+            if (a->data_type->class > HLSL_CLASS_VECTOR)
+                return false;
+            component_size = a->data_type->e.numeric.type == HLSL_TYPE_DOUBLE ? sizeof(double) : sizeof(uint32_t);
+            for (i = 0; i < a->data_type->e.numeric.dimx; ++i)
+            {
+                if (memcmp(&x->value.u[i], &y->value.u[i], component_size))
+                    return false;
+            }
+            return true;
         }
         case HLSL_IR_LOAD:
         {
